pingo-ptbr-edge is the microcontroller edition of pingo-ptbr (https://huggingface.co/semfence/pingo-ptbr): a Brazilian Portuguese
text-to-speech model whose acoustic part is stored in 4 bits per weight and whose vocoder is a reduced FARGAN (109,733 parameters)
trained from scratch by SemFence, with a C inference runtime and an ESP32-S3 firmware project.

The architecture of the vocoder is the FARGAN vocoder of Xiph/Opus (BSD-3-Clause) with narrower layers. No weights of the
original FARGAN or of PiVo are used by this edition: the reduced vocoder was trained from random initialization.
Its notices are in LICENSES/. The acoustic design follows PiVo-1.4M (Empero Research, Apache-2.0); its acoustic weights are
trained from scratch by SemFence (see semfence/pingo-ptbr).

The weights are licensed under CC BY 4.0 (credit required: SemFence, Gustavo Toledo). The code is licensed under Apache-2.0.
The FARGAN-derived code keeps its BSD-3-Clause license.
